From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: report the GPU module's own answer

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: when the native GPU backend found nothing, ffDetectGPU went on to
Vulkan, OpenCL and OpenGL fallbacks and then said "GPU detection failed",
hiding why. None of those fallbacks is built for AROS.
Solution: on AROS return the native backend's message.
Scope: detection/gpu/gpu.c, AROS only.
Upstream-Status: AROS-specific.
Verification: --show-errors -s GPU on pool v1-1, v11-1 and rpi-1
(2026-10-27): "GPU: Not supported on AROS".
Removal: with an AROS GPU backend, or with upstream AROS support.
---
 src/detection/gpu/gpu.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c b/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c
index 7031368..b1e266d 100644
--- a/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c
+++ b/src/detection/gpu/gpu.c
@@ -255,6 +255,11 @@ const char* ffDetectGPU(const FFGPUOptions* options, FFlist* result) {
         FF_DEBUG("PCI/native GPU detection did not produce results (error=%s, gpuCount=%u)",
             error ?: "none",
             result->length);
+#ifdef __AROS__
+        // No Vulkan, OpenCL or OpenGL fallback is built for AROS: the
+        // native answer is the one to report.
+        return error ?: "No GPU found";
+#endif
     }
     if (options->detectionMethod <= FF_GPU_DETECTION_METHOD_VULKAN) {
         FF_DEBUG("Trying Vulkan GPU detection fallback");
